# Project memory - deliberately kept out of the product repository.
#
# Reason: untouchable rule 7 - the language criterion is PLACE, not audience.
# Everything inside the repository is English; these files are in the owner's
# language, so they cannot live here. Their history is kept in a separate,
# private repository rooted at docs/.
#
# Consequence to remember: ripgrep and the Grep tool honour this file, so the
# whole project memory is invisible to a directory-wide search. Name the path
# explicitly (docs/, CLAUDE.md) or use Select-String, which reads what it is told.
docs/
tools/
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG-DEV.md

# Memory attributes file - see the comment inside it.
# If the product ever needs its own line-ending rules, uncomment this entry and
# merge the rules deliberately instead of creating a second file.
.gitattributes

# Rust build output. Regenerated by every build, never edited by hand.
/target/
**/target/

# Editor and formatter leftovers.
**/*.rs.bk

# Debug symbols produced by the MSVC toolchain on Windows.
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS tracked on purpose - do not add it here.
#
# This project ships two executables, so it is an application, not a library.
# The Cargo FAQ notes that `cargo new` tracks the lockfile by default and that
# it buys deterministic builds across machines and time, which is exactly what
# a release needs: the same bytes from the same tag. For a library the lockfile
# would not affect consumers, so the trade-off would be different - it is not.
